<reading-questions xml:id="reflections-more-det">
<title>Reflect on your understanding</title>

<introduction><p>
	In addition to the reflection activities below,
	re-read <xref ref="section-more-det-terminology" text="type-global-title" />.
	Be sure you understand each of the new definitions introduced in this chapter,
	and spend some time committing them to memory.
</p></introduction>

<exercise>
	<title>The role of the adjoint matrix</title>

	<introduction><p> Consider the formula <m>A (\adj A) = (\det A) I</m>. </p></introduction>

	<task><p>
		Briefly explain why the formula is true for all square matrices.
		(Do not assume the size of the matrix <mdash /> your explanation should be equally valid for <em>all</em> sizes of square matrices.)
	</p></task>

	<task><p> Briefly explain the relationship between this formula and the concept of <term>matrix inverse</term>. </p></task>

</exercise>

<exercise>
	<title>Determinants of row equivalent matrices</title>
	<p> Explain why the determinants of two row equivalent matrices must be either both zero or both nonzero. </p>
</exercise>

<exercise>
	<title>Cramer's rule</title>
	<p> Briefly summarize Cramer's rule and how it follows from the adjoint inversion formula. </p>
</exercise>

</reading-questions>
